  ],
  "equipment_type": "Variable frequency drive",
  "applies_to": "Fuji Electric FRENIC-Eco HVAC drives fitted with the OPC-F1-BAC BACnet MS/TP option card in option port A.",
  "summary": "The OPC-F1-BAC card gives the FRENIC-Eco a BACnet MS/TP port. It maps the drive's communication command words (S06/S07), status words (M13/M14) and monitor values to fixed objects: BVs for run/reverse/reset commands, drive status bits and the X-terminal link commands, BIs for the final X-terminal states, BOs for the Y and 30 relay outputs, AVs for frequency, current, voltage, temperatures, hour meters and fault history, plus select/value AV pairs that read or write any parameter by group.",
  "bacnet_transport": [
    "BACnet MS/TP"
  ],
  "firmware": null,
  "default_device_instance": "37000 + address DIP switch value (37000-37255)",
  "access_inferred": false,
  "notes": [
    "Object list from the Start-Up Guide FECA-IN-112 (pages 6-9); the linked drive registers in the descriptions and the units come from the I/O Map Addendum FECA-TE-124 (https://americas.fujielectric.com/files/Frenic%20Eco%20Bacnet%20I_O%20Map%20Addendum%20FECA-TE-124.pdf).",
    "The guide's unit column repeats the object name for the parameter select/value AVs and for AV 42-45; the addendum leaves those units blank, which is used here.",
    "BV 4 is printed with the same name as BV 1 (Reverse_Command); the addendum links it to the reverse-rotation status bit (M14 bit 1), so it is a read-only status.",
    "BV 16-22 hold the X1-XR terminal states written through the link (S06); BI 0-6 show the terminal states the drive actually uses (M13). Write BV 16-22 to drive a terminal over BACnet MS/TP.",
    "Parameter access: write the parameter number to a *_Parameter_Select AV (e.g. AV 14 = 5 for S05), then read or write the matching *_Parameter_Value AV. An unsupported parameter returns 0 with reliability set to fault."
  ],
  "integration": {
    "summary": "Fit the card in option port A, set the device instance and baud rate on its DIP switches, set the Y-codes as listed in the guide and set H30 so frequency and run commands come from the link, then restart the drive. Command BV 0 forward run and write the frequency reference to AV 0 (Hz); reset trips with BV 2. Read BV 3, AV 2, AV 30, BV 13 and AV 7.",
    "minimum_points": [
      {
        "ref": "BV 0",
        "name": "Forward_Command",
        "why": "Run forward command (1 = run)"
      },
      {
        "ref": "AV 0",
        "name": "Frequency_Command_Setpt",
        "why": "Frequency reference in Hz"
      },
      {
        "ref": "BV 2",
        "name": "Alarm_Reset",
        "why": "Resets a drive alarm"
      },
      {
        "ref": "BV 3",
        "name": "Forward_Rotation",
        "why": "Running forward status"
      },
      {
        "ref": "AV 2",
        "name": "Frequency_Command",
        "why": "Frequency command in use, Hz (M05)"
      },
      {
        "ref": "AV 30",
        "name": "Output_Current_Real",
        "why": "Output current in amps"
      },
      {
        "ref": "BV 13",
        "name": "Alarm_Relay",
        "why": "Alarm relay active (drive alarm)"
      },
      {
        "ref": "AV 7",
        "name": "Latest_Alarm",
        "why": "Latest alarm code"
      }
    ],
    "enable": "H30 selects where the frequency and run commands come from; the guide's example ('H30=-8') gives both frequency and run command control over BACnet MS/TP. Restart the drive after setting it. BV 14 Communications_Act shows when the link commands are in effect.",
    "heartbeat": null,
    "remote_sensors": "AV 1 PID_cmd (S13) takes a PID command from the BMS when the drive's PID is used.",
    "setup": [
      "Device instance: address DIP switches A0-A7 give 37000-37255.",
      "Baud rate DIP switches B0-B4: 9600, 19200, 38400, 76800 or auto.",
      "Terminating and bias resistor DIP switches are on the card; turn them on at the end of the line if needed.",
      "Guide's Y-code settings: Y01 = 1, Y02 = 0, Y03 = 2, Y04 = 4, Y05 = 0, Y06 = 0, Y07 = 1, Y08 = 0, Y09 = 0.01, Y10 = 0; Y11-Y20 the same; Y98 = 0, Y99 = 0.",
      "The OPC-F1-RS option card may have to be removed to fit the OPC-F1-BAC."
    ],
    "gotchas": [
      "AV 5 Output_Current is in % of rating; use AV 30 Output_Current_Real for amps.",
      "Writes through the *_Parameter_Value AVs change drive parameters; don't write them cyclically.",
      "BV 4 shares its object name with BV 1; tell them apart by instance.",
      "Use either a link command (BV 16-22) or the terminal for each X input, not both."
    ]
  },
  "source": {
    "title": "Fuji BACnet (OPC-F1-BAC) Start-Up Guide for the Fuji Electric FRENIC-Eco VFD",
